WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:03.120
Jackie Burkhart was a career-defining role for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:06.780
Mila Kunis, but there's something she&nbsp;
finds unnerving about "That '70s Show."

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:12.480
Regarded as one of the funniest sitcoms in TV&nbsp;
history, "That '70s Show" appeals to audiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:18.000
young and old with its nostalgic subject matter&nbsp;
and endearing portrayal of teenage life. As such,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.660
it's no wonder that the show's immense&nbsp;
popularity helped launch the careers of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:25.500
its young cast which included the likes&nbsp;
of Ashton Kutcher, Wilmer Valderrama,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.920
Laura Prepon, Topher Grace,&nbsp;
and of course, Mila Kunis.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:33.360
Kunis, in particular, has enjoyed an enormous&nbsp;
amount of success since her breakout role as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.800
Jackie Burkhart in "That '70s Show," scoring a&nbsp;
recurring role on "Family Guy" as the voice of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.760
Meg Griffin and starring in prolific films&nbsp;
such as "Forgetting Sarah Marshall," "Black&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:47.040
Swan," and "The Book of Eli." Considering the&nbsp;
many notable and successful projects she has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:51.720
been involved in since the 2006 conclusion of&nbsp;
"That '70s Show," it might surprise some fans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:56.700
to learn that she actually refuses to watch the&nbsp;
series for one admittedly understandable reason.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.800
During an appearance on the "Happy&nbsp;
Sad Confused" podcast in October 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.520
Mila Kunis confessed that she has&nbsp;
never actually seen a full episode&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:09.960
of "That '70s Show." The actor went on&nbsp;
to explain that she finds it too odd&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.680
to see her most awkward teenage years&nbsp;
preserved on camera for all to watch.

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:18.960
Kunis' reluctance makes sense when considering&nbsp;
the fact that she infamously lied about her age&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:24.420
to join "That '70s Show," jumping onto the main&nbsp;
cast when she was just 14 years old. Where most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.140
people might get away with simply avoiding&nbsp;
old yearbook photos or trying not to remember&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:33.060
their awkward phases from high school, Kunis has&nbsp;
several full seasons of television that document&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:38.100
her teenage years. Still, while she may prefer not&nbsp;
to spend a lot of time revisiting her adolescence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:42.480
the actor isn't completely opposed to giving&nbsp;
"That '70s Show" a shot. As she explained,

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:46.800
"If it ever goes back to broadcast, and if&nbsp;
it comes on, then I think I'd watch it."

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:51.420
While Mila Kunis hasn't watched "That '70s Show,"&nbsp;
it doesn't appear to have anything to do with her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:55.860
experience working on the show itself. In&nbsp;
fact, the actor has spoken quite positively&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.860 --> 00:01:59.700
about the filming environment for the series.&nbsp;
She shared in an interview with Vanity Fair,

00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:03.900
"I had the greatest experience on&nbsp;
''70s.' 100 percent, I was embraced."

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:08.160
"I was never treated as lesser-than,&nbsp;
and if I did by one of the cast members,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.660
another cast member would stand up for it."

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:13.140
Kunis has also talked about how difficult&nbsp;
it was to leave the show behind when it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:16.800
came time for the finale in 2006.&nbsp;
Kunis said on "The Ellen Show,"

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.560
"On the day, I couldn't stop crying. I literally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.380
reverted to being a little kid and&nbsp;
I just wanted someone to hold me."

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:26.280
But while the program may have ended,&nbsp;
the story of Jackie Burkhart didn't.

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:29.940
Though it took over a decade and a&nbsp;
half for the opportunity to arise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:34.320
Mila Kunis didn't turn down the chance&nbsp;
to play the iconic character once again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:38.220
She and her husband Ashton Kutcher, who&nbsp;
portrayed Michael Kelso in the original series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:44.100
returned to their classic roles for Netflix's&nbsp;
2023 spin-off "That '90s Show." Jackie and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.660
Kelso pop up in the first episode of Season 1,&nbsp;
appropriately titled "That '90s Pilot," with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:52.260
the latter giving Kurtwood Smith's Red&nbsp;
Forman a headache for old times' sake.

00:02:52.260 --> 00:02:54.240
While Kunis admitted to Access Hollywood&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:57.780
that it was a strange experience to be&nbsp;
filming opposite her husband once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:02.580
she lavished praise on the overall production.&nbsp;
Prior to the show's debut, the actress said,

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:06.840
"It's very sweet. It pays&nbsp;
homage to anyone who's ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:11.100
watched ''70s' or loved '70s Show,'&nbsp;
they will be really happy with it."

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:16.080
At the same time, considering that Jackie ends&nbsp;
up with Wilmer Valderrama's Fez in the "That '70s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:21.000
Show" finale, Kunis does find it a bit odd that&nbsp;
Jackie and Kelso are an item in "That '90s Show."

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.240
At the end of the day, even though&nbsp;
she hasn't gone back to watch it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:29.580
"That '70s Show" will always remain a standout&nbsp;
part of Mila Kunis' career and pop culture legacy.

